      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0395-p00835",
      "source_en": "(page 61)\nMy deer and hound are properly related to the deer and hound that Ricker in\nand out of the various tellings of the Arthurian legends, leading different knights\nupon adventures, and to the hounds and to the hornless deer at the beginning\nof, I think, all tellings of Oisin's journey to the country of the young. The hound\nis certainly related to the Hounds of Annwoyn or of Hades, who are white, and",
